Dear Stefan,

Let us look at the three appendix tables at the long table from 10.00 next Th=
ursday, 16 April. I have attached the short note on how I propose to use each=
 one: the receipt quarters, the grounds for counting, and the name references.

Could you particularly try the six same-spelling entries against the leaves a=
nd lines? I want to know whether each can be found separately, even where we =
cannot establish that two entries refer to the same person. The note lists th=
e three pairs to start with.

Thank you,
Judith


